        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Thanks for the PR!\r\n> \r\n> This indeed caused problems once or twice before (but allowed to find issues with other modules, but not really important).\r\n\r\nProbably it doesn't matter much assuming using `make_notify` wrapper. I found the problem when I tried to call `update()` inside `vim.ui_attach` callback (probably especially if `return_prompt` event causes waiting for `<CR>` input). Example (with modified mini.notify): https://github.com/przepompownia/mini-ui-messages-example\r\n\r\n> I think I'd prefer to have `refresh()` itself schedule its effects depending on whether currently inside fast event. Not sure about the best approach yet, though.\r\n\r\nDo you mean the `if not vim.in_fast_event()` logic could be placed inside `M.refresh()`? I considered it at the start but didn't found any simpler approach than the current.",
